ke how Han said first time but I  love that you said Falcon on stage  that's our celebration which is how I  [Laughter]  know but here's what we didn't know who  the heck is playing Lando Calrissian  well this was an awesome day it was  October 2016 it was a Friday I think  like maybe four or five in the afternoon  I'm packing up to leave for the day and  then Lucasfilm is like  lmao you're not leaving for the day  because we're gonna announce Lando right  now on a Friday afternoon great for the  media loves when this happens Donald  Glover Donald Glover Glover amazing  casting and let's round out some of the  other casting here that came out around  the same time we've got Woody Harrelson  reportedly playing a character named  Beckett maybe Tobias Beckett this is all  kind of speculation but Beckett was a  name that Woody Harrelson actually  dropped in an interview Emilia Clarke  has reportedly named Kyra  I've seen like nine different spellings  of this but she's brunette with bangs  Tandy Newton unknown character Phoebe  Waller bridge also unknown reportedly a  CG driven character and Michael K  Williams had originally been cast but he  was reportedly removed from the film the  final film after being unable to return  to set for pick ups which brings us to  the director shake-up they shot a heck  of a lot of the movie up until June 2017  when it was announced that Lord and  Miller were fired citing creative  differences president of Lucasfilm  Kathleen Kennedy said in a statement  quote Phil Lord and Christopher Miller  are talented filmmakers who have  assembled an incredible cast and crew  but it's become clear that we had  different creative visions on this film  and we've decided to part ways a new  director will be announced soon  Lorna Miller were also quoted in the  statement saying unfortunately our  vision and process weren't aligned with  our partners on this project we normally  aren't fans of the phrase creative  differences but for once this cliche is  true we are really proud of the amazing  and world-class work of our cast and  crew only two days later Ron Howard was  announced as the director who would take  the reins and steer this consolo ship  into  this is where I admittedly became pretty  doubtful of the Han Solo movie it just  seemed all over the place I mean they  didn't push back the release which we  thought they would and I'm a huge fan of  Lord Millar I love their work and I  wanted to see what they would have done  with the movie and their kind of comedic  style  Ron Howard just seemed like the complete  opposite of that and it seemed like this  whiplash in tone and didn't really know  what was happening there  however devil's advocate on myself  Ron Howard seemed to work overtime to  ease our minds he posted photos from set  seemingly as often as he could he even  added some unexpected legends characters  like tag and Bank who appear to be silly  comedic comics in the early 2000s and  with each passing day I got more and  more on board with Ron Howard's Han Solo  movie I'm in for it  so around this time he added some more  people to the cast we've got Paul  Bettany we've got Warwick Davis and Ron  Howard's brother Clint Howard filming  for the project wrapped in October 2017  and that's when Ron Howard announced the  official title solo a Star Wars story  I'm fine with it now let's talk about  the score the quick and dirty on Star  Wars scores all over the board is that  they're John Williams babies they're all  John Williams but not the standalone  movies rogue one was composed by Michael  Giacchino and Han Solo will be composed  by John Powell John Powell scored a ton  of movies How to Train Your Dragon the  United 93 or some good ones to start if  you kind of want to google them YouTube  and listen to him for a minute check  those out but however in December as in  a few weeks ago John Williams was giving  an interview to Variety where he said  that he would write the theme for Han  Solo while John Powell will write the  rest of the score so what can we see in  the Han Solo movie this is where I got  doubtful because I'd liked the idea that  Han Solo is this legend that may or may  not have lied his way into the Star Wars  universe lied his way into the rebellion  it's like oh you've never heard of the  Millennium Falcon this is the ship that  made the Kessel run in less than 12  parsecs was he lying about that probably  I mean I liked the idea that he could  have lied or embellished his way into  the Alderaan mission to get money and  then was reluctantly thrust into the  Star Wars and eventually became a war  hero  I mean I don't really need to see how  that happened but we are likely getting  the Kessel run and how Han Solo won the  Millennium Falcon from Lando which I  like I like that I would like to see  that because it seems like the Falcon  belongs to land over much of the film  we've seen that shot of the Wardrobe  that he has inside it's like this nice  pristine Falcon and then maybe Han gets  it and it's also rumored that Jabba the  Hutt will appear in the film it's clear  they have this long history when we  first hear of him or see him if you're  watching the special editions but I  don't know what are your hopes and  wishes for Solo a Star Wars story let us  know in the comments or you can hop on  Twitter where I'm a Jedi in the streets  but a sit in the tweets see you next  time may the force be with you

